                <pb facs="0911" n="823" sameAs="frus:frus1904/pg823"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Loomis to Mr. Leishman.</hi></head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Telegram.—Paraphrase.]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of State</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1904-07-16"><hi rendition="#italic">July 16,
                        1904</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p>(Mr. Loomis instructs Mr. Leishman to ask an Imperial audience at a fixed day and
                    hour in the near future, and to state to the minister for foreign affairs that
                    the Government of the United States fails to understand the delay in according
                    him the treatment due to the friendly relations of the two countries.)</p>
            </div>
        </body>
